**Rules:**
- Validate and bind input before touching anything else; reject malformed input
  with the project's 400 response shape.
- <!-- FILL: the exact binding/validation call to use and the one to reject
     (many frameworks ship a convenience binder that silently writes an error
     response or aborts — name which is which). -->
- <!-- FILL: how to read the authenticated principal, set by your auth
     middleware, and what to do when it is absent. -->
- Parameterized queries only — never build SQL by string formatting or
  concatenation with request data.
- Release every acquired resource on all paths (result sets, file handles,
  locks, spans).
- Wrap errors with context as they propagate, preserving the original for
  sentinel matching.
- Always return immediately after writing a response — never fall through into
  a second write.
- Client-facing error messages stay generic; details go to the log, not the
  response body.

